    "title": "Planned Parenthood of Illinois names new president - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CHICAGO (WMBD) — Planned Parenthood will soon have some new leadership in Illinois. Adrienne White-Faines will be taking over as the new president and CEO of Planned Parenthood of Illinois and Planned Parenthood Illinois Action in September, Planned Parenthood spokesperson MJ Maharry said. She will be replacing the Interim President Tonya Tucker, who took over after the previous president, Jennifer Welch, stepped down in January. “PPIL has a strong history of providing safe and effective reproductive care to improve health and well-being for patients across Illinois”, White-Faines said. “Having devoted my career to advancing health for all populations, through education, patient services, public policy, research and training, I am honored now to carry forth in this mission with PPIL and PPIA, to address the needs of individuals for generations to come!” Maharry said White-Faines recently served as the Chief Strategy Officer for the American College of Physicians. She also previously served as the Chief Executive Officer of the American Osteopathic Association and the Vice President and Chief Health Officer for the American Cancer Society’s Illinois Division. More information on Planned Parenthood of Illinois is available here . For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CIProud.com.",
